WEBVTT

00:01.435 --> 00:03.765
shinjitai
I want to believe

00:03.795 --> 00:06.995
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light that I found that day

00:07.435 --> 00:10.165
kimi to kawashita
Because I still have

00:10.205 --> 00:14.905
tatta hitotsuno yakusoku ga arukara
That one promise that I made to you

00:15.275 --> 00:23.155
mou tachidomarazuni aruite yukitai
I want to keep walking, never stopping

00:23.185 --> 00:26.845
Dragon Drive

00:26.885 --> 00:32.325
uresugita kajitsu wo kajiru youni
Like biting into an overripe fruit

00:32.725 --> 00:35.425
yowai jibun ni
I was spoiling myself

00:35.465 --> 00:38.695
amaetsuzukete ita
I was giving in to my weakness

00:39.235 --> 00:43.225
kimi ni deawanakereba
If I hadn't met you

00:43.505 --> 00:45.475
ima mo
I'd still...

00:45.505 --> 00:51.875
kabe wo kowasu koto nado dekinakatta yo
...be unable to break the walls around me

00:53.585 --> 00:55.885
wasurenai
I'll never forget

00:55.915 --> 00:59.255
ano hi kanjita itami
The pain that I felt that day

00:59.525 --> 01:04.225
nido to ano basho modoritakunai
I never want to go back to that place

01:04.425 --> 01:05.855
motto tsuyoku
This strong feeling

01:06.125 --> 01:08.525
shinjitai
I want to believe

01:08.635 --> 01:11.795
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light I found that day

01:12.135 --> 01:17.125
kakkowarui to warawaretemo ii
Let them laugh and call me a loser

01:17.305 --> 01:19.795
bukiyou dakara
Because I'm clumsy

01:20.075 --> 01:27.885
onaji ikikata shika erabenainda
I can only choose to live life this way

01:53.005 --> 01:53.975
Mukai.

01:57.245 --> 01:59.185
Let's go home, guys.

01:59.645 --> 02:00.615
Huh?

02:01.585 --> 02:06.025
Why should we hafta bother with some guy
who showed off and got himself killed?

02:06.555 --> 02:07.715
Kyoji!

02:08.125 --> 02:10.255
Don't tell me you actually mean
what you said!

02:10.395 --> 02:12.255
Yeah, I mean it.

02:12.725 --> 02:14.715
It's how I feel. I'm serious.

02:15.065 --> 02:17.295
How could you? That's too cruel!

02:17.495 --> 02:19.895
Mr. Mukai fought with all his might!

02:20.405 --> 02:22.465
Right. Like he wanted.

02:23.175 --> 02:25.435
He selfishly showed off and died,
against everyone's will.

02:25.775 --> 02:27.265
Kyoji!

02:27.345 --> 02:29.105
Just leave that guy alone.

02:29.515 --> 02:33.745
He's probably finally with his mother,
letting her spoil him.

02:34.785 --> 02:36.375
Just let him do as he wishes.

02:36.515 --> 02:38.955
That's enough, already!

02:40.485 --> 02:41.755
Do as you wish.

02:42.495 --> 02:44.755
You never told us anything.

02:45.995 --> 02:48.515
I thought we were friends, weren't we?

02:50.495 --> 02:51.525
Kyoji.

02:57.305 --> 03:00.295
I will never forget you, Mukai.

03:00.905 --> 03:02.535
The time we fought with each other.

03:03.075 --> 03:04.605
The fact that you were strong.

03:05.345 --> 03:06.375
I will never forget.

03:10.485 --> 03:13.645
The Journey

03:14.595 --> 03:16.055
Mukai is dead.

03:16.695 --> 03:18.995
If this were a game,
he could easily come back to life.

03:19.025 --> 03:22.325
But before we knew it,
our battle had ceased to be a game.

03:23.195 --> 03:24.185
Chibi.

03:24.705 --> 03:26.425
When I first met you...

03:26.835 --> 03:30.275
...little did I dream that anything
like this would happen.

03:37.275 --> 03:39.375
I might've slept too much.

03:39.615 --> 03:41.375
My head hurts.

03:43.955 --> 03:45.415
Before I met Chibi...

03:45.985 --> 03:48.425
...I couldn't get serious about anything.
- Hey, that's dangerous!

03:48.795 --> 03:51.585
I was known as the guy
who could never finish what he started.

03:58.365 --> 03:59.955
What did you do that for?!

04:00.765 --> 04:04.295
Wait, aren't you the King of Tardiness
from Class B?!

04:04.975 --> 04:06.465
This place, here! Hurry!

04:06.575 --> 04:07.575
Ryugujo: The Sea Palace

04:07.575 --> 04:10.045
Ryugujo: The Sea Palace
What's with this rundown cheap candy store?

04:10.045 --> 04:10.515
Ryugujo: The Sea Palace

04:10.515 --> 04:12.315
Ryugujo: The Sea Palace
Can't you read the sign above?

04:12.315 --> 04:12.385
Ryugujo: The Sea Palace

04:12.385 --> 04:14.545
Ryugujo: The Sea Palace
Ryu-gu-jo?

04:14.715 --> 04:16.415
Right! Here we go, Mr. Turtle!

04:18.985 --> 04:20.385
Come on, this way!

04:20.685 --> 04:21.585
H-Hey!

04:21.625 --> 04:23.115
You can't just walk into someone's home!

04:23.395 --> 04:24.855
Especially with muddy shoes!

04:25.125 --> 04:28.155
- Maiko Yukino, a childhood friend of mine...
- Press this, and?

04:28.535 --> 04:30.895
...introduced me to the game Dragon Drive.

04:31.605 --> 04:34.005
The closet's an elevator?

04:34.135 --> 04:36.865
Two people on our way to the Ryugujo!

04:40.005 --> 04:42.475
What in the world?

04:46.445 --> 04:49.005
Now, for our next participant! Let's do it!

04:49.355 --> 04:51.685
Welcome, Reiji Ohzora!

04:51.925 --> 04:53.445
Ah? Um, yeah.

04:55.095 --> 04:56.755
This one!

04:57.355 --> 04:58.555
Dragon Drive.

04:58.595 --> 04:59.065
All right!

04:59.095 --> 05:01.465
It is a game where the players
ride realistic dragons...

05:01.495 --> 05:04.265
...and battle in realistic towns.
- Th-This is the dragon sleeping within me?

05:05.005 --> 05:07.865
Chibi was the dragon selected for me.

05:07.975 --> 05:09.965
I-It really is sleeping!

05:10.505 --> 05:13.235
Now, then. Commencing Dragon Drive!

05:13.605 --> 05:15.445
D-Break!

05:24.285 --> 05:25.515
It's pitch black.

05:35.335 --> 05:36.665
A-A city?!

05:38.505 --> 05:40.265
Ouch!

05:40.665 --> 05:42.635
What was that?!

05:44.175 --> 05:45.435
Th-This guy.

05:46.275 --> 05:48.605
It's the dragon they were calling my partner.

05:52.245 --> 05:53.505
Wh-Wh-Wha...

05:53.985 --> 05:55.815
What's that thing?!

05:57.955 --> 05:59.475
Remember, Chibi?

05:59.825 --> 06:02.585
The very first time,
you were really weak and timid...

06:02.625 --> 06:04.525
...so we couldn't even put up a decent fight.

06:04.995 --> 06:08.195
But you showed me
determination not to lose.

06:08.535 --> 06:12.995
And seeing you like that,
I didn't wanna lose, either.

06:13.035 --> 06:14.025
Chibi.

06:14.335 --> 06:16.275
Are you attacking?!

06:19.005 --> 06:20.835
He was so frightened a moment ago.

06:21.205 --> 06:23.575
He doesn't wanna lose, either.

06:23.915 --> 06:27.345
But all I was thinking about
was how to escape.

06:29.255 --> 06:30.375
You're right!

06:30.715 --> 06:32.315
We can't run away any longer!

06:32.525 --> 06:35.495
Let's do what we can
to sock him a good one!

06:37.725 --> 06:39.215
Take this!

06:46.005 --> 06:47.465
Wh... Wh...

06:47.735 --> 06:49.795
What?!

06:50.035 --> 06:52.905
That ball of fire should hit
from this distance!

06:53.275 --> 06:55.005
Do it!

07:09.495 --> 07:11.485
I-I thought I'd die.

07:18.205 --> 07:19.255
Daisuke!

07:22.435 --> 07:26.875
Kanper ignored my orders to evade
the foe, and is fighting on his own.

07:27.445 --> 07:29.635
As a result, his hit points are close to zero.

07:29.715 --> 07:31.475
What a dimwitted dragon.

07:32.085 --> 07:33.745
It's game over, no matter how you slice it.

07:34.385 --> 07:36.075
We won't know until we try!

07:37.255 --> 07:40.225
I made a decision that with this game...

07:40.485 --> 07:42.925
...I'll never hit the reset,
no matter how close I come to losing!

07:48.735 --> 07:50.495
Elemental Shift!

07:52.935 --> 07:55.365
Ever since I began fighting with Chibi...

07:55.605 --> 07:57.165
...I've encountered a number of people.

07:57.735 --> 07:58.935
Daisuke Hagiwara.

07:59.645 --> 08:02.905
At first, I thought he was a little strange...

08:02.945 --> 08:04.635
...with his little theories about Maiko and me.

08:05.045 --> 08:06.775
But soon I noticed a similarity to me.

08:07.515 --> 08:10.115
I felt he was someone I could fight with.

08:11.525 --> 08:12.505
What speed!

08:21.165 --> 08:23.135
That girl had already given up!

08:23.435 --> 08:25.765
Why did you have to finish that dragon off?

08:25.965 --> 08:29.735
You'd better worry about yourself
before worrying about others.

08:30.335 --> 08:32.605
Judging from your reaction,
you'll never survive the game.

08:42.085 --> 08:44.845
Reiji Ohzora, show me one more time.

08:45.625 --> 08:46.985
Show me your power.

08:48.925 --> 08:50.945
Chibi's... trembling.

08:56.135 --> 08:57.495
Reiji!

08:57.595 --> 08:58.395
Sayaka!

08:58.435 --> 09:00.365
Please catch me!

09:12.385 --> 09:14.575
A-A-A-Are you okay?!

09:14.715 --> 09:17.045
Yes! I'm safe, thanks to you!

09:18.925 --> 09:20.915
I also met many strong people.

09:21.495 --> 09:22.475
Ichirou.

09:22.595 --> 09:23.585
Kyoji.

09:23.825 --> 09:24.815
Sayaka.

09:25.565 --> 09:29.995
And also the ultimate super-champion
of Dragon Drive, Hikaru Himuro.

09:30.895 --> 09:31.885
Mr. Himuro!

09:32.505 --> 09:33.835
It's Hikaru Himuro!

09:33.865 --> 09:35.865
The first time I fought against Hikaru...

09:36.105 --> 09:38.365
...I was no match for him.

09:38.975 --> 09:41.675
I felt that I didn't wanna lose to him,
no matter what.

09:42.215 --> 09:43.195
Chibi.

09:43.345 --> 09:46.835
I genuinely felt that I wanted
to become stronger, together with you.

09:47.215 --> 09:48.405
Where are we going?

09:48.455 --> 09:50.075
The special training room.

09:50.255 --> 09:51.245
Special?

09:51.385 --> 09:52.975
For special members only.

09:53.325 --> 09:55.555
That's where Himuro trained as well.

09:55.795 --> 09:56.585
He did?

09:57.125 --> 09:59.355
Way to go, Chibi! Go! Go!

10:00.195 --> 10:02.285
Get him now! Go for it!

10:02.435 --> 10:05.335
You're doing good! Chibisuke!

10:05.535 --> 10:07.965
You must first observe your opponent...

10:08.335 --> 10:09.805
...and learn its weakness.

10:10.135 --> 10:11.865
That's it, Chibi! The belly button!

10:12.605 --> 10:14.665
- I felt so strongly about defeating Hikaru...
- Go after his belly button!

10:14.705 --> 10:17.645
...that I went to Miss L and asked
that we receive special training.

10:18.385 --> 10:19.905
I was amazed.

10:20.245 --> 10:22.345
As we began gaining strength...

10:22.385 --> 10:25.475
...Chibi was no longer the cute little Chibi
I had known, but a big dragon.

10:27.355 --> 10:28.825
Eww... What is this?!

10:28.995 --> 10:33.365
- At first, I couldn't believe...
- Wh-What's going on? M-My body's!

10:33.365 --> 10:35.725
...that it was your true appearance.
- This time I can hear it clearly.

10:35.895 --> 10:37.095
I was so thrilled...

10:37.135 --> 10:39.535
...to see you become a really strong Chibi.

10:40.265 --> 10:41.255
Chibi.

10:41.435 --> 10:44.095
You truly were a sleeping dragon
waiting to be woken up.

10:45.675 --> 10:51.165
But there were others
also waiting for you to awaken.

10:52.185 --> 10:54.345
Your awakening was the key...

10:55.055 --> 10:57.955
...that brought us to this world.
- She's calling me.

10:58.725 --> 11:02.085
This other Earth, Rikyu.

11:18.705 --> 11:21.575
The world we were brought to
was an alternate Earth...

11:22.315 --> 11:25.835
...a world where dragons live, Rikyu.

11:25.985 --> 11:29.475
I am the one who drew you into this world.

11:30.455 --> 11:32.475
What is this place?

11:32.855 --> 11:33.845
Rikyu.

11:34.085 --> 11:36.955
There is a parallel world that exists
in a dimension separate from Earth.

11:37.655 --> 11:41.495
The only thing that can save Rikyu,
the whole world itself...

11:41.735 --> 11:43.925
...is the power of Senkohcoola.

11:44.565 --> 11:48.165
It is all in order to protect
the Dragonite from RI-ON.

11:48.265 --> 11:49.665
W-Wait a minute!

11:49.705 --> 11:52.465
This "Senkohcoola" and "Dragonite"...

11:52.675 --> 11:54.935
What are you talking about?!

11:55.175 --> 11:56.835
Long ago...

11:57.015 --> 11:59.915
...our world Rikyu
faced a terrible and dangerous threat.

12:00.845 --> 12:03.015
A most powerful dark dragon...

12:03.215 --> 12:05.615
...Shinryu descended upon the land.

12:06.085 --> 12:10.755
It was then that the Dragon of Light,
Senkohcoola, appeared.

12:11.555 --> 12:17.225
After a long battle, Senkohcoola was able
to trap Shinryu in the Dragonite.

12:18.365 --> 12:21.895
However, RI-ON hopes
to acquire that Dragonite...

12:21.975 --> 12:24.375
...and aims to resurrect Shinryu.

12:25.075 --> 12:28.375
RI-ON seeks to use Shinryu's power
to achieve their goal...

12:28.515 --> 12:31.675
...of dominating the two worlds,
both the Earth and Rikyu.

12:36.355 --> 12:37.945
What's this supposed to be?!

12:38.215 --> 12:40.345
Is that all the guardian god can do?!

12:40.485 --> 12:41.685
What's the matter, Chibi?

12:42.755 --> 12:43.955
You're weak!

12:43.995 --> 12:45.685
You're too weak!

12:50.135 --> 12:51.995
Lightning Wave!

12:52.265 --> 12:53.255
What?!

12:53.565 --> 12:56.405
Rockaku's the first friend I made in Rikyu.

12:57.175 --> 13:00.575
He loves to drink and easily gets into fights,
but he's a great guy.

13:01.475 --> 13:03.065
Although he's somewhat older than me.

13:05.685 --> 13:07.545
You're strong.

13:07.985 --> 13:11.885
It seems that you're not the boy
I thought you were.

13:12.255 --> 13:14.485
You're a solid man!

13:16.225 --> 13:17.785
You'd better win.

13:18.195 --> 13:19.185
All right?

13:20.925 --> 13:21.415
Y-Yes!

13:21.765 --> 13:24.755
It was then determined that Maiko, Daisuke
and I would join Rockaku...

13:24.795 --> 13:27.495
...and participate in Dragonic Heaven.
- Hold it!

13:27.805 --> 13:30.535
- All to prevent RI-ON from
getting their hands on the Dragonite.
- How can you do such a horrible thing?!

13:30.575 --> 13:33.645
This dragon is a toy that we found.

13:33.645 --> 13:35.305
- During the preliminary match...
- What we do with it...

13:35.345 --> 13:38.075
...I met the twins Lin and Sue.
...has nothing to do with you.

13:38.075 --> 13:40.945
- These two were being controlled by RI-ON.
- What?! You're calling Chibi a toy?!

13:41.915 --> 13:44.245
Using even children as tools to their benefit...

13:44.585 --> 13:47.285
...and when such tools became useless,
they were discarded like garbage.
- What's this light?!

13:47.655 --> 13:49.815
- That's the kind of cruel organization
that RI-ON is.
- I-It feels creepy!

13:49.855 --> 13:52.195
Vanish into the light, Darks!

14:05.245 --> 14:09.105
We will now begin the first match
of the second round!

14:12.285 --> 14:13.835
It's not just Kyoji.

14:14.145 --> 14:16.045
Sayaka's also participating
in the tournament.

14:16.285 --> 14:18.985
Wh-What's that girl doing here?!

14:19.555 --> 14:23.255
What a surprise to see both Kyoji
and Sayaka here in Rikyu.

14:23.555 --> 14:27.285
Not only that, but for us to face off
against them in Dragonic Heaven?

14:28.125 --> 14:33.465
Through this match, I learned that RI-ON
wasn't the only one wanting the Dragonite.

14:52.955 --> 14:53.945
It's fast!

14:54.185 --> 14:55.885
The Dragonite is mine!

14:56.195 --> 14:57.315
I won't let anyone else get it!

14:57.595 --> 14:59.355
I cannot let anyone else get it!

14:59.395 --> 15:02.955
If you want your mother back,
get the Dragonite.

15:03.335 --> 15:05.625
So says Mr. Guan-Coo.

15:06.305 --> 15:07.325
Mother!

15:07.505 --> 15:08.625
Mukai!

15:08.905 --> 15:10.025
Guan-Coo!

15:10.235 --> 15:11.865
Just make sure you keep your promise!

15:17.475 --> 15:18.845
I will not be defeated.

15:20.115 --> 15:21.775
I cannot allow myself to be defeated!

15:27.755 --> 15:28.745
Please.

15:29.125 --> 15:30.115
Give this to Mukai.

15:38.135 --> 15:40.155
Wh-What's wrong, Shadow Fang?!

15:40.665 --> 15:41.935
We can't lose!

15:42.335 --> 15:44.035
I must win this bout!

15:44.875 --> 15:46.675
This'll end it!

15:50.675 --> 15:51.665
Mukai.

15:52.545 --> 15:54.415
Please stop fighting.

15:54.945 --> 15:56.575
Mother.

16:05.195 --> 16:06.185
Game over.

16:06.525 --> 16:10.655
It wasn't only Kyoji and Sayaka
who had come here to Rikyu.

16:10.695 --> 16:13.635
RI-ON had sent people here
as part of their plan to get the Dragonite.

16:14.065 --> 16:16.625
Ichirou Sumishiba, Hikaru Himuro...

16:17.035 --> 16:18.905
...and Kouhei Toki.

16:22.615 --> 16:25.275
Not yet! I will not be defeated!

16:25.685 --> 16:27.405
Until I avenge my mother's death...

16:27.445 --> 16:29.435
...and the destruction of my village...

16:29.915 --> 16:32.115
...I cannot and will not die!

16:38.425 --> 16:40.985
Let's go, Thundervolt!

16:57.245 --> 16:59.075
Let me fight, too!

16:59.285 --> 17:02.075
Let me avenge Yakou's death!

17:03.755 --> 17:05.375
Shadow Fang!

17:06.825 --> 17:09.285
Hearing that Mukai was in great danger
after going off to fight Guan-Coo...

17:09.755 --> 17:11.745
...we decided to try to rescue him.

17:12.595 --> 17:14.785
I couldn't ignore the fact he was in trouble.

17:15.465 --> 17:16.955
I brought backup!

17:17.335 --> 17:18.325
What?!

17:20.165 --> 17:21.655
Are you all right, Mukai?!

17:22.305 --> 17:23.135
Reiji.

17:23.235 --> 17:24.865
What are you doing here?!

17:25.305 --> 17:27.205
I need no help!

17:27.345 --> 17:28.675
Don't be so stubborn.

17:28.745 --> 17:30.405
They're friends we fought against.

17:30.845 --> 17:31.835
Friends?

17:31.915 --> 17:33.315
That's right, Mukai!

17:33.685 --> 17:37.175
A friend of Kyoji is a friend of mine!

17:40.985 --> 17:41.925
Now, Mukai!

17:42.095 --> 17:43.255
Guan-Coo!

17:43.495 --> 17:45.425
Take this!

17:55.165 --> 17:56.465
You mustn't go.

17:56.705 --> 17:58.675
You mustn't touch the Dragonite!

17:59.345 --> 18:01.745
How dare you give me orders?!

18:06.645 --> 18:09.085
I now have my last item.

18:11.215 --> 18:13.985
We're now entering the final stage.

18:16.555 --> 18:19.655
Rockaku could only watch
as Kouhei became champion...

18:19.865 --> 18:21.855
...and took the Dragonite.

18:22.595 --> 18:23.585
The Dragonite...

18:24.035 --> 18:25.895
...became RI-ON's possession.
- What's so funny?!

18:27.565 --> 18:31.505
Whaddaya say I test the powers
of this thing?

18:31.835 --> 18:32.565
What?!

18:53.565 --> 18:55.795
Oh, no!

18:59.265 --> 19:00.795
Wow.

19:01.465 --> 19:04.135
This thing has some incredible powers.

19:04.475 --> 19:06.205
Awesome!

19:08.445 --> 19:09.205
Go!

19:15.455 --> 19:16.435
What?!

19:35.135 --> 19:36.335
M-Mukai!

19:36.775 --> 19:38.795
If you injured yourself fighting recklessly...

19:38.875 --> 19:41.345
...or got killed trying to get revenge...

19:41.675 --> 19:43.735
...would that make
Reiji and the others happy?!

19:49.185 --> 19:51.275
If I lost my life in order to defeat this guy...

19:51.315 --> 19:52.875
...that's a trade I'd be satisfied with!

19:53.025 --> 19:54.855
You're getting on my nerves.

19:55.325 --> 19:56.315
Disappear, already!

20:01.595 --> 20:02.585
Mukai!

20:17.415 --> 20:20.005
Mukai! Hang on! Hey!

20:25.415 --> 20:26.515
What is it?

20:30.555 --> 20:33.155
Mukai lost his life in this battle.

20:33.565 --> 20:35.465
That was a lot of fun.

20:35.865 --> 20:37.025
Nice work!

20:37.495 --> 20:41.765
We did everything we could
to get the Dragonite from Kouhei...

20:42.335 --> 20:43.235
...but we failed to do so.

20:45.205 --> 20:47.765
B-Bastard!

20:48.475 --> 20:49.775
Rockaku!

20:52.445 --> 20:53.705
Are you all right?

20:55.855 --> 20:57.075
Kouhei!

20:57.115 --> 20:59.785
Kouhei!

21:05.895 --> 21:08.155
We lost this battle.

21:08.865 --> 21:10.295
It's all over.

21:10.595 --> 21:11.895
No, it isn't over!

21:16.135 --> 21:17.365
I will not give up.

21:17.735 --> 21:21.195
I will be sure to find a way
to get the Dragonite back!

21:21.375 --> 21:22.745
B-But you know...

21:22.845 --> 21:24.575
It's over the moment we give up!

21:24.915 --> 21:28.075
I will never push that reset button
no matter what happens!

21:28.345 --> 21:29.545
I will never give up!

21:30.455 --> 21:31.245
Right!

21:31.785 --> 21:33.945
I still haven't had my revenge yet!

21:34.255 --> 21:35.445
I won't give up, either!

21:35.795 --> 21:37.085
Just watch us, Mukai!

21:37.595 --> 21:40.755
We will be sure to get the Dragonite back!

21:55.915 --> 21:58.645
taikutsu datta
I was bored

21:58.675 --> 22:01.345
okubyou datta
I was a coward

22:01.385 --> 22:05.285
dareka wo jibun wo kizutsukete ita
I was hurting someone and myself

22:06.825 --> 22:09.515
tsuyogari itte
I tried to hide my weakness

22:09.555 --> 22:12.115
wagamama itte
I was being selfish

22:12.195 --> 22:16.225
doushiyoumonai kimochi mamoritsuzukete
Protecting the uncontrollable feeling

22:17.765 --> 22:20.395
otona ni natte
I became an adult

22:20.435 --> 22:23.135
kimi to deatte
Then I met you

22:23.175 --> 22:27.305
mune no sumikko yawarakaku natte
My heart got softened

22:28.475 --> 22:31.005
setsunaku natta
Longing for love

22:31.345 --> 22:33.315
dakishime atta
We embraced each other

22:33.985 --> 22:39.005
hakkiri mamorubeki mono wo mitsuketa
I finally knew what I wanted to protect

22:39.485 --> 22:42.215
tatta hitotsu no yuuki ga
Only one courage

22:42.255 --> 22:44.725
tatta hitotsu no kotoba ga
Just one word

22:44.995 --> 22:49.725
futari owaranai yume e to hakobu
Take us to an endless dream

22:50.435 --> 22:53.095
hon no chiisana yasashisa ga
Only a small kindness

22:53.135 --> 22:55.605
hon no wazuka na sasayaki ga
Only a small whisper

22:55.875 --> 23:00.675
futari wo sotto tsutsunde kureru
Wrap us gently

23:01.105 --> 23:05.515
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:06.515 --> 23:12.145
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:14.655 --> 23:16.795
Next time

23:16.795 --> 23:17.355
Next time
What?!

23:17.355 --> 23:18.295
What?!

23:18.325 --> 23:21.095
RI-ON may return to Rikyu?!

23:21.825 --> 23:23.295
And to prepare for this...

23:23.335 --> 23:25.395
...we're to search for others to help
in our battle against RI-ON?!

23:26.205 --> 23:27.665
Well, leave it to me!

23:27.805 --> 23:31.035
Or so I thought, but Chibi's fallen ill!

23:32.375 --> 23:34.435
What?! He could die
unless we do something about it?!

23:34.475 --> 23:35.275
You're kidding!

23:35.305 --> 23:37.865
Next, on Dragon Drive, "Rebirth".

23:38.075 --> 23:39.175
Wait a minute.

23:39.345 --> 23:41.685
Does that mean I get a new partner
in the next episode?!

23:41.685 --> 23:42.285
Rebirth
Does that mean I get a new partner
in the next episode?!

23:42.285 --> 23:44.375
Rebirth
Tell me it ain't so!
